Mobile screenshot 390x844 actually rendered at 780x1688 (device scale). HUD bars are hidden behind controls indeed: health text "100" at bottom center, bars overlap joystick/attack. Boss chest glow still huge (this screenshot maybe before latest changes? The server HMR should have latest; but mobile screenshot taken after edits? Yes after chest changes? It still shows giant glow. Hmm maybe chestGlow not the source. It could be aura still. Wait we changed chestGlow to .68 color and aura moved behind. The screenshot still has a giant bright orb at chest center. Maybe it's the `aura` sprite at z=-1.1 but camera sees it behind torso; bloom makes it visible through? Sprite is additive and depthWrite false, but depthTest true by default. It should be occluded by torso. It appears centered on chest and huge, possibly `this.light` reflecting. Or the `weaponTipGlow` at weapon? No.

Actually the glow might be the moon behind the boss! Look at screenshot: a huge circular glow at center above boss. Wait the moon is at (-46,48,-92) left side; but in portrait view, boss center, there's a large ring (gate rose window) behind and a bright orb at center? The gate's roseGlow is at y14.2, behind boss, appears as a huge halo. But the bright orb at chest is not moon. It could be boss aura. Let's determine by hiding objects in page and screenshot. We can identify mesh/sprite. Use raycast? Or toggle. Let's run a quick test in browser, set `boss.aura.visible=false`, `chestGlow.visible=false`, `light.intensity=0`, screenshot. Compare. We can inspect screenshot maybe. We'll use a script that captures crops? Simpler screenshot with aura hidden.

Also mobile HUD needs fix. On portrait, move player bars above touch controls, perhaps at bottom 160px? But controls occupy bottom 200. We can place `.hud-bottom` bottom: 200px on max-width 560/portrait; bars on left? Or move player panel to top-left under boss plate? Better in portrait: player bars at top left, under act/boss? Boss plate center top; run readout top right. Put bars at left under boss plate? Could overlap. Maybe at bottom center above controls: `.hud-bottom { bottom: 190px; left: 0; right:0; justify-content:center; padding-bottom:0; } .player-panel { ... } .bars { width: 55vw; }` But bars then sit above controls, around y=620, okay. It might obscure boss feet but fine. Or place at top-left at y=90. Typical mobile games put health top-left, but boss bar top center. Could put player HP under act badge? On mobile act badge hidden. Top-left area free. Use `.hud-bottom { top: max(80px,...); bottom:auto; align-items:flex-start; }` with boss plate centered. The bars would be under top-left, not conflict. But the parry prompt is at 54%, fine. On 390 width, boss plate 242px centered x74-316. Bars width 164, x? left 14, could overlap boss plate horizontally? boss plate top 14-69; bars top 80, below. Good. But the boss plate height 55, so bars at y=80. Player panel bars width 42vw=164, x14. The right side run readout top right maybe. This seems good: player HP top-left, boss bar top-center, timer top-right. But the HUD bottom controls removed from bottom. The player panel includes sigil, bars, flasks. At top-left, could overlap act badge (hidden) and run readout? Bars width 164, top 80. Fine.

However in landscape (844x390), top-left bars might be fine too. But current landscape bars at bottom-left and controls right; no overlap. Keep bottom for landscape. Use media `(orientation: portrait) and (max-width: 900px)` to reposition.

Actually CSS `@media (max-width: 560px)` currently applies to portrait 390. Add:
```
@media (max-width: 620px) and (orientation: portrait) {
 .hud-bottom { top: max(78px, calc(env(safe-area-inset-top) + 70px)); bottom: auto; padding: 0 14px; align-items: flex-start; }
 .player-panel { gap: 8px; }
