content.text:
Landscape mobile looks good overall, but touch controls overlay bars? Bars x81-360, joystick x22-146, overlap! In landscape, bars at bottom-left y330, joystick y252-376 x22-146; bars x81-360 y330-380. Overlap. The player bars are partly behind joystick. In screenshot, the "VITALITY" label and left part of HP bar are behind joystick. Need fix for touch landscape too. The current media query only portrait. For landscape mobile (max-width 900 and touch), we should reposition bars above joystick or top-left. The landscape viewport 844x390; vertical space limited. The bars could be at bottom center between joystick and touch-right? x150-600 width 450, y330. Touch-right x620-826. That could work: `.hud-bottom { left: 155px; right: 220px; bottom: 10px; } .bars { width: 100%; }`. But player-panel includes sigil; joystick occupies left. Could hide sigil and place bars center-left at x160. In screenshot, bars from x81 to 360; moving to x160 gives room. Better: for touch landscape, set `.hud-bottom { left: 158px; right: 220px; bottom: max(14px,...); } .player-panel { width:100%; } .bars { width:100%; } .player-sigil { display:none; }`. At 844 width, left 158 right 220 => 466px width. Bars 466, good. But touch-right x620-826, so right edge 624, slight overlap; right 230 -> 614. Good. Bottom y330. Joystick ends 376; bars 330-380 but x>158 no overlap. Touch-right starts x620. Fine. The control hints hidden. The health bar would be at x158-624, good. The player panel sigil hidden. The flask row. This works.

But what about tablets landscape 1024x768 touch? The media max-width 900 doesn't apply, touch controls visible via pointer coarse, bars bottom-left width 33vw=338, joystick 124 x22-146, bars x46? overlap. For touch landscape generally, need layout. Add `@media (pointer: coarse) and (orientation: landscape)` with reposition. But the touch controls display only if body.playing.touch; pointer coarse. Use `@media (pointer: coarse) and (orientation: landscape)`.
```
.hud-bottom { left: 160px; right: 240px; bottom: max(12px, env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); justify-content: flex-start; }
.player-panel { width:100%; }
.player-sigil { display:none; }
.bars { width: 100%; max-width: 420px; }
.control-hints { display:none; }
```
But on a 1024x768 tablet, right 240 leaves 624 width, bars max 420. Good. On 844x390, width 444. Good. The bars might still overlap touch-right if right 240 and touch-right width 206 at right 18 => starts x620 on 844, our right edge 604. Good. On 1024, touch-right starts 800, bars max 420 at x160 -> 580. Fine.
Need player panel at bottom, flask row. Fine.

Also touch controls in landscape overlap the bottom right but okay.

Add CSS.

